vm.field.ip.restart.dhcp.modal.content:
After a online IP address change, you need to enter the VM console and run the following command to restart the DHCP Client.

- Linux VMs:
	- If the network is not managed by NetworkManager, run the following command: dhclient -r ${ifname}; dhclient ${ifname}
	- If the network is managed by NetworkManager, run the following command: nmcli c up ${ifname}
- Windows VMs: Enter the command line tool and run the following command: ipconfig /release && ipconfig /renew

vmNic.modal.set.ipAddress.console.curl.a:
To make the modification take effect, you need to enter the console of the VM instance and run the following command to restart its DHCP service :

- Linux VM instance:
  - If the network is not managed by NetworkManager, the command is: dhclient -r ${ifname}; dhclient ${ifname}
  - If the network is not managed by NetworkManager, the command is: nmcli c up ${ifname}
- Windows VM instance: Enter the command line tool and run the following command: ipconfig /release && ipconfig /renew

